735	/* ================================================================== *
736	 * The rate-limit key was a field the caller filled in
737	 *
738	 * nginx forwards `X-Forwarded-For: $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for`, which APPENDS
739	 * the peer it saw to whatever the caller sent. So the LEFTMOST entry is
740	 * caller-authored text, and `(xff ?? "").split(",")[0]` — the expression that
741	 * keyed the login, register, password-reset, verification-resend and wallet
742	 * top-up throttles — returns whatever the caller typed.
743	 *
744	 * Measured through the real staging nginx: 25 POSTs with a rotating
745	 * X-Forwarded-For never tripped a 20/minute limit that a fixed value trips on
746	 * the 21st, and a forged value was written verbatim into the visitor log.
747	 * ================================================================== */
748	
749	/** `(…get("x-forwarded-for") …).split(",")[0]` in any spelling. */
750	const LEFTMOST_XFF = /x-forwarded-for[\s\S]{0,120}?\.split\(","\)\s*\[\s*0\s*\]/;
751	
752	/**
753	 * Call sites that STILL derive the caller's address from the leftmost hop, with
754	 * the owning file. This list is an inventory of remaining exposure, not an
755	 * approval: the assertion is a SUBSET check, so fixing one shrinks it and the
756	 * suite stays green, while introducing a NEW one turns it red.
757	 *
758	 * `lib/actions.ts` is the one that matters most and is not fixed here because it
759	 * was owned by another change in flight: `login` keys its throttle this way, so
760	 * the 10-attempts-per-15-minutes lockout that is supposed to stop password AND
761	 * 2FA guessing against a named account can be stepped around by varying a
762	 * header. Replace each with `clientIp(await headers())` from lib/rate-limit.ts.
763	 */
764	const XFF_STILL_OUTSTANDING = new Set([
