850	 * A session cookie and an impersonation cookie are the same kind of string
851	 *
852	 * Both are HS256 over the same AUTH_SECRET, so `jwtVerify` accepts either in
853	 * either slot. Nothing distinguished them, so moving the value of
854	 * `nxeon_session_imp` into `nxeon_session` produced a genuine session as the
855	 * impersonated customer — not flagged as impersonation, so no banner, and
856	 * `audit()` stops appending `actingAdmin=…`. Every action after that is recorded
857	 * as the customer's own.
